WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.835
Security dashboards often contain sensitive material: video, internal addresses,

00:00:04.835 --> 00:00:08.600
usernames, facility layouts, device details, and investigation notes.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.600
Access should be based on job need, not simple convenience.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.415
Role-based access can separate operators, investigators, administrators, auditors,

00:00:16.415 --> 00:00:17.520
and read-only viewers.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.215
Apply least privilege to both people and services.

00:00:20.215 --> 00:00:24.320
A user who reviews endpoint alerts may not need unrestricted video access.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.085
A collector that submits events does not need permission to administer the dashboard.

00:00:28.085 --> 00:00:31.100
Review access regularly and remove stale accounts promptly.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.590
Retention policies define how long logs, clips, thumbnails, notes,

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.425
and audit records remain available.

00:00:36.425 --> 00:00:38.590
Different data types may require different periods.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:42.400
Keep data long enough for legitimate security, legal, and operational needs,

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.020
but do not preserve sensitive material indefinitely without a defined reason.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.915
Minimize or mask data where full detail is unnecessary.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:53.100
A dashboard may display an event category and time without a persistent face image,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.400
or restrict raw clips to authorized review.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.800
Local-only storage can reduce external disclosure when remote processing is not required,

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.160
but it still needs encryption, backup, and physical protection as appropriate.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.610
Audit logs should record sign-ins, searches, exports, configuration changes,

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:10.750
administrative actions, and access to especially sensitive evidence.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:15.760
Protect those logs from casual alteration and review them for misuse or unexpected access.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.160
Responsible policy defines approved purposes, prohibited monitoring,

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:22.200
notice where required, review procedures, and accountability.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.640
Do not use the dashboard for stalking, harassment, covert surveillance,

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.075
or identification of private individuals without lawful authority and a legitimate need.

00:01:30.075 --> 00:01:34.200
Privacy is an architectural and operational requirement, not an optional disclaimer.
